{"name":"build-locale-pages.md","path":"jsdocs/shared/scripts/build/build-locale-pages.md","format":"markdown","html":"<article class=\"docs-md\"><h1 id=\"sharedscriptsbuildbuild-locale-pagesmjs\"><code>shared/scripts/build/build-locale-pages.mjs</code></h1>\n<p>Emits per-locale, per-route static index.html files into</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Source</strong></td>\n<td><code>src/shared/scripts/build/build-locale-pages.mjs</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>UX surface</strong></td>\n<td>The repo verbs — build, verify, test, docs, i18n, media, setup, scaffold.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"members\">Members</h2>\n<h3 id=\"slugify\"><code>slugify</code></h3>\n<p>Media-slug transform — MUST match generate-sitemap.js&#39;s slugify byte for\nbyte: emitted /portfolio/<slug>/<media> file names have to line up with\nthe URLs the sitemap already lists (diacritics fold to ASCII).</p>\n<h3 id=\"esc\"><code>esc</code></h3>\n<p>Escape a string for use inside an HTML attribute or text node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"todescription\"><code>toDescription</code></h3>\n<p>Strips markup from a translated rich-text string and compacts it into a\nmeta-description-sized plain-text snippet (≤160 chars, cut at a word\nboundary). &nbsp; entities decode to regular spaces so the tag can sit\nin a content attribute.</p>\n<h3 id=\"breadcrumbentity\"><code>breadcrumbEntity</code></h3>\n<p>Ordered crumbs → BreadcrumbList entity (positions are 1-based per spec).</p>\n<h3 id=\"videoentity\"><code>videoEntity</code></h3>\n<p>VideoObject for one media descriptor — mp4 contentUrl + poster thumb.</p>\n<h3 id=\"module-scope\">(module scope)</h3>\n<p>Recursively yields every sections node that carries a <code>src</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"writecompressed\"><code>writeCompressed</code></h3>\n<p>Brotil + gzip siblings next to each emitted index.html (Firebase serves them).</p>\n<h3 id=\"localize\"><code>localize</code></h3>\n<p>Rewrites the English shell into a localized document.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} html - post-loader dist/index.html source</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {object} o</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} o.bcpLang - BCP-47 tag for <html lang> + og:locale alt</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} o.ogLocale - og:locale value (xx_YY)</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} o.title - document + social title</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} o.description - meta description text</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} o.url - this page&#39;s absolute URL</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} [o.canonicalUrl] - canonical/og:url override for alias pages</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {Array&lt;{bcp:string,url:string}&gt;} o.alternates - hreflang rows</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} [o.image] - route-specific share image (project cover /</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {Array<object>} [o.entities] - extra JSON-LD entities appended to</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"buildlocalepages\"><code>buildLocalePages</code></h3>\n<p>Generates all localized pages under <code>distDir</code>. When <code>template</code> is omitted\nthe post-loader dist/index.html is read from disk; when provided (the\nbuild orchestrator&#39;s in-memory copy) the localized root document is\nreturned so the caller can run its own compress/SW-stamp pass.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} distDir - absolute dist path</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} [template] - shell HTML; defaults to dist/index.html on disk</li>\n<li><code>@returns</code> {{html: string, written: number, locales: number}} localized root html + counts</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"t\"><code>t</code></h3>\n<p>Per-locale lookup with English fallback (mirrors runtime appText).</p>\n<h3 id=\"firstpara\"><code>firstPara</code></h3>\n<p>Recursively finds the first paragraph string inside a nested sections payload.</p>\n<h3 id=\"projectentities\"><code>projectEntities</code></h3>\n<p>Full rich-media graph for one project page — Article + media\nItemList (entries deep-link to the emitted /portfolio/<p>/<media>\nURLs; the SPA serves every labelled media slug) + one VideoObject\nper video. Mirrors runtime generateProjectSchema.</p>\n<h3 id=\"projectimageof\"><code>projectImageOf</code></h3>\n<p>Cover share-image for a project — uncompressed jpg or video poster.</p>\n<h3 id=\"homeentities\"><code>homeEntities</code></h3>\n<p>Carousel ItemList for locale home pages — portfolio tiles → covers.</p>\n<h3 id=\"pagenamefromtitle\"><code>pageNameFromTitle</code></h3>\n<p>Strips the <code>Luis Krötz | </code> prefix / <code> | Luis Krötz</code> suffix for crumb names.</p>\n<h3 id=\"mediarowsof\"><code>mediaRowsOf</code></h3>\n<p>Expandable-media {slug,label,media} rows of a project — mirrors generate-sitemap&#39;s walk.</p>\n<h3 id=\"routesfor\"><code>routesFor</code></h3>\n<p>Route table: relative path → title, localized description,\ncanonical-equivalent alternates path, optional canonical override.\n<code>path</code> is the emitted file path relative to its base (en → dist/,\nothers → dist/langs/); en home yields &#39;&#39; — dist/index.html is\nalready written by the root pass.</p>\n<h3 id=\"syncfirebaserewrites\"><code>syncFirebaseRewrites</code></h3>\n<p>Regenerates the <code>hosting.rewrites</code> block in firebase.json so the public\nlocale URLs (<code>/br</code>, <code>/br/sobre</code>, …) keep serving the pages now emitted\nunder <code>dist/langs/&lt;loc&gt;/…</code>. Firebase rewrite destinations are single\nfiles — no glob capture — so the table enumerates every route the same\nway <code>routesFor</code> does. Preserves every non-rewrite hosting key and the\nmeta/CMS/SPA-catch-all entries declared in <code>STATIC_REWRITES</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"meta_file_rewrites\"><code>META_FILE_REWRITES</code></h3>\n<p>Rewrites that sit before the locale table — meta files moved into\npublic/meta/ keep their root URLs through these entries. Per-locale\nsitemap files and localized agent-readable files (robots/urllist/llms/\nai-catalog under /meta/<loc>/) keep their <code>/&lt;loc&gt;/&lt;file&gt;</code> URLs.</p>\n<h3 id=\"spa_rewrites\"><code>SPA_REWRITES</code></h3>\n<p>CMS + SPA catch-all — always last.</p>\n</article>","mtime":"2026-10-14T06:02:55.461Z"}